{
  "title": "'It Was Horrible': Farah Khan Opens Up About Postpartum Body Changes And Tummy Tuck Surgery",
  "publication_date": "2026-07-27T10:33:36Z",
  "summary": "Filmmaker-choreographer Farah Khan spoke openly about her post-pregnancy body changes, saying \"It was horrible.\" She explained why she chose to have a tummy tuck years after giving birth to triplets and that it took her seven years to regain her fitness.",
  "content": "Filmmaker-choreographer Farah Khan recently spoke candidly about her post-pregnancy transformation, describing the period after childbirth as difficult and saying \"It was horrible.\" In public comments, she explained why she underwent a tummy tuck several years after giving birth to triplets and reflected on the long process of recovery and self-care.\n\nAccording to her account, the journey back to fitness was gradual and took about seven years. Farah emphasized the physical and emotional challenges she faced during that time, noting that regaining strength and confidence did not happen overnight and required sustained effort.\n\nShe framed the decision to have a tummy tuck as a personal one, made after weighing the impact of childbirth on her body and her own well-being. While she did not go into surgical detail in the remarks cited, her openness contributes to wider conversations about postpartum health, body image and the choices some parents make to address lasting physical changes.\n\nFarah's comments also highlight how celebrity experiences can spark public discussion about the realities of motherhood beyond the early postnatal period. By sharing that her recovery spanned years, she underscored that long-term healing and fitness are common elements of many parents' journeys.\n\nSource lines included with the original report read: \"CWG 2026 News\" and \"Latest Blogs.\" The report lists the author as \"Unknown Author\" and the original summary information as \"Unknown\" for publication date in its metadata.\n",
